{
  "dom_id": "step-q171780",
  "name": "Question 14",
  "problem": "$\\,$ If $x$ is divisible by $6,$ then $x$ is even.\n\nWhich of the following is logically equivalent to the conditional predicate above?",
  "worked_solution": "Let's denote by $P(x)$ and $Q(x)$ the following predicates:\n\n- $P(x):$ $x$ is divisible by $6.$\n\n- $Q(x):$ $x$ is even.\n\nThen, our initial sentence can be written as $P(x)⇒Q(x),$ which is logically equivalent to \n\n$$\n¬P(x)∨Q(x).\n$$\n\nThe negation of $P(x)$ can be written as\n\n- $¬P(x):$ $x$ is not divisible by $6.$\n\nTherefore, the given sentence is logically equivalent to the following:\n\n$\\,$ $x$ is not divisible by $6,$ or $x$ is even.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
